1","pocket":"security"}]},"type":"USN","cves":[{"id":"CVE-2026-106553","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106552","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106585","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106583","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106584","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106586","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106587","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106555","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-106582","notices_ids":["USN-8928-1","USN-8937-1"]}],"cves_ids":["CVE-2026-106553","CVE-2026-106552","CVE-2026-106585","CVE-2026-106583","CVE-2026-106584","CVE-2026-106586","CVE-2026-106587","CVE-2026-106555","CVE-2026-106582"],"releases":[{"codename":"stonking","version":"26.10","support_tag":""}],"related_notices":["USN-8928-1"]},{"id":"USN-8936-1","title":"PHP vulnerabilities","summary":"Several security issues were fixed in PHP.","instructions":"In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.","references":[],"published":"2026-10-19T13:25:32.204359","description":"It was discovered that PHP did not properly validate the size of MySQL\nserver packets in the mysqlnd driver. A malicious server could possibly use\nthis issue to cause PHP to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This\nissue was only addressed in Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu\n24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2025-1218)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled response buffer sizes in the\nSOAP HTTP client. A malicious server could possibly use this issue to cause\nPHP to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2025-14181)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled certain TAR archive headers\nin the Phar extension. An attacker could possibly use this issue to inject\narbitrary files into a crafted archive. (CVE-2026-6103)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP did not limit recursion depth when parsing\ncertain SOAP requests. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause PHP to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-91765)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled authentication headers when\nfollowing HTTP redirects. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-91766)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled wildcard names in TLS server\ncertificates. A malicious server could possibly use this issue to cause PHP\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue did not affect\nUbuntu 14.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-91767)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly validated IPv6 client addresses in\nthe FastCGI client access check. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to bypass access restrictions. This issue did not affect Ubuntu 14.04\nLTS. (CVE-2026-91768)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly performed TLS peer name\nverification. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\nimpersonate a trusted server. (CVE-2026-91769)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled certain stream filter\noptions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive\ninformation. (CVE-2026-92842)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled empty Location headers when\nfollowing HTTP redirects. A malicious server could possibly use this issue\nto redirect the client to an unintended location. This issue did not affect\nUbuntu 14.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-93682)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"bionic":[{"name":"php7.2","version":"7.2.24-0ubuntu0.18.04.17+esm13","description":"HTML-embedded scripting language interpreter","is_source":true},{"name":"libapache2-mod-php7.2","version":"7.2.24-0ubuntu0.18.04.17+esm13","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/php7.2","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"libphp7.2-