Several security issues were fixed in RabbitMQ Server.","instructions":"In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.\nAfter a standard system update you need to restart rabbitmq-server to make\nall the necessary changes.","references":[],"published":"2026-10-15T17:27:24.712969","description":"It was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled CORS wildcard\norigin configuration. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\na cross-site request forgery attack. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04\nLTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04\nLTS. (CVE-2026-66070)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled TLS\npeer-certificate DNs in the management UI. An attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause a cross-site scripting attack. (CVE-2026-66077)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled AMQP 1.0 arrays\nwith zero-width element constructors. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 20.04\nLTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-66079)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server trust-store plugin incorrectly\nvalidated client certificates. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\nbypass TLS client authentication. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-67231)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled WebSocket frame\nsizes. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67232)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled content-header\nbody sizes. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-67235)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly stored credentials in an\ninsecure cookie. An attacker could possibly use this issue to expose\nsensitive information. This issue only affected Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu\n22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67236)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled OAuth bearer\ntokens in bootstrap JavaScript. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a cross-site scripting attack. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67237)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled ETF-encoded PID\nnode names. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67238)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled TLS\npeer-certificate DNs in the stream management UI. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a cross-site scripting attack. This issue\nonly affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-67239)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled OAuth2 SSL\noptions when no CA certificates were available. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to bypass TLS verification. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67404)\n\nIt was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly validated HTTP response\nstatus codes when fetching JWKS keys. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04\nLTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-67409)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"bionic":[{"name":"rabbitmq-server","version":"3.6.10-1ubuntu0.5+esm1","description":"AMQP server written in Erlang","is_source":true},{"name":"rabbitmq-server","version":"3.6.10-1ubuntu0.5+esm1","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/rabbitmq-server","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-in