e":false,"is_visible":false,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23/1.23.1-1~22.04.3","pocket":"security"},{"name":"golang-1.23-go","version":"1.23.1-1~22.04.3","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23/1.23.1-1~22.04.3","pocket":"security"},{"name":"golang-1.23-src","version":"1.23.1-1~22.04.3","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/golang-1.23/1.23.1-1~22.04.3","pocket":"security"}]},"type":"USN","cves":[{"id":"CVE-2026-39821","notices_ids":["USN-8416-1","USN-8883-1","USN-8900-1","USN-8914-1","USN-8883-2"]}],"cves_ids":["CVE-2026-39821"],"releases":[{"codename":"jammy","version":"22.04","support_tag":"LTS"}],"related_notices":["USN-8416-1","USN-8883-1","USN-8900-1","USN-8914-1"]},{"id":"USN-8916-2","title":"PyJWT vulnerabilities","summary":"Several security issues were fixed in PyJWT.","instructions":"In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.","references":[],"published":"2026-10-15T06:24:37.994435","description":"USN-8916-1 fixed vulnerabilities in PyJWT. This update provides the\ncorresponding fix for PyJWT on Ubuntu 26.10.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\nYuSung Han discovered that PyJWT did not properly validate certain JWK keys\nwhen performing HMAC verification. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to forge authentication tokens. (CVE-2026-102266)\n\nRohan Das discovered that PyJWT incorrectly handled redirects when fetching\nkey sets. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to  cause PyJWT\nto disclose sensitive information. (CVE-2026-102267)\n\nIt was discovered that PyJWT incorrectly recognized certain PEM\nrepresentations. An attacker who knew the public key could possibly use\nthis issue to forge authentication tokens. (CVE-2026-102268)\n\nNuno Lopes discovered that PyJWT incorrectly handled DER public keys when\nperforming HMAC verification. An attacker who knew the public key could\npossibly use this issue to forge authentication tokens. (CVE-2026-102271)\n\nIt was discovered that PyJWT did not properly handle certain JWK keys\nprefixed with a byte-order mark. An attacker who knew the public key could\npossibly use this issue to forge authentication tokens. (CVE-2026-102272)\n\nCharles Vosburgh discovered that PyJWT incorrectly handled certain JWK\ncontainers when performing HMAC verification. An attacker who knew the\npublic key could possibly use this issue to forge authentication tokens.\n(CVE-2026-102273)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"stonking":[{"name":"pyjwt","version":"2.13.0-1ubuntu1","description":"Python 3 implementation of JSON Web Token","is_source":true},{"name":"python-jwt-doc","version":"2.13.0-1ubuntu1","is_source":false,"is_visible":false,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/pyjwt","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/pyjwt/2.13.0-1ubuntu1","pocket":"security"},{"name":"python3-jwt","version":"2.13.0-1ubuntu1","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/pyjwt","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/pyjwt/2.13.0-1ubuntu1","pocket":"security"}]},"type":"USN","cves":[{"id":"CVE-2026-102268","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-102271","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-102272","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-102273","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-102267","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-102266","notices_ids":["USN-8916-1","USN-8916-2"]}],"cves_ids":["CVE-2026-102268","CVE-2026-102271","CVE-2026-102272","CVE-2026-102273","CVE-2026-102267","CVE-2026-102266"],"releases":[{"codename":"stonking","version":"26.10","support_tag":""}],"related_notices":["USN-8916-1"]},{"id":"USN-8932-1","title":"curl vulnerabilities","summary":"Several security issues were fixed in curl.","instructions":"In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.","references":[],"published":"2026-10-14T19:26:26.170504","description":"Stanislav Fort discovered that curl did not properly clear AWS SigV4\nauthentication state when CURLOPT_AWS_SIGV4 was set to NULL. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information. This\nissue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-86409)\n\nStanislav Fort discovered that an HTTP proxy could trick libcurl into\nsending credentials to the proxy itself by responding to a CONNECT\nrequest with an unexpected authentication challenge. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information.\n(CVE-2026-86414)\n\nStanislav Fort discovered that curl did not correctly handle HSTS\nentries when an includeSubDomains parent entry was imported before a\nlonger-lived child entry. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause curl to use unencrypted HTTP connections. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-87862)\n\nStanislav Fort discovered that curl did not properly handle HSTS max-age\nvalues that exceeded calendar time structure bounds. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or data loss. This\nissue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-87863)\n\nStanislav Fort discovered that curl did not properly handle IMAP APPEND\ncommands when CURLOPT_CRLF was enabled, allowing overflow bytes to be\ninterpreted as pipelined commands. An authenticated attacker could\npossibly use this issue to inject arbitrary IMAP commands.\n(CVE-2026-87864)\n\nJoshua Rogers discovered that libcurl had a use-after-free vulnerability\nin the FTP wildcard matching code. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause curl to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\nexecute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-92388)\n\nJoshua Rogers discovered that libcurl's TFTP state machine did not\nproperly validate transfer directions, allowing a malicious server to\nforce the client into transmit mode. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-92389)\n\nJoshua Rogers discovered that curl had a stack overflow vulnerability\nwhen processing deeply nested MIME structures. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause curl to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-92391)\n\nJoshua Rogers discovered that libcurl could expose credentials in the\nURL returned by CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL when credentials were retrieved\nfrom a .netrc file. An attacker could possibly use this issue to obtain\nsensitive information. This issue only affected Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu\n22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-94266)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"bionic":[{"name":"curl","version":"7.58.0-2ubuntu3.24+esm15","description":"HTTP, HTTPS, and FTP client and client libraries","is_source":true},{"name":"curl","version":"7.58.0-2ubuntu3.24+esm15","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/curl","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"libcurl3-gnutls","version":"7.58.0-2ubuntu3.24+esm15","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/curl","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"libcurl3-nss","version":"7.58.0-2ubuntu3.24+esm15","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/curl","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"libcurl4","version":"7.58.0-2ubuntu3.24+esm15","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/curl","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"libcurl