bly use this\nissue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-63292)\n\nLucian Nitescu and Zhen Kong discovered that Apache HTTP Server did not\nproperly handle certain responses from backend servers. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-63686)\n\nQing Xu discovered that Apache HTTP Server incorrectly interpreted HTTP\nresponses from backend servers. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to perform HTTP response smuggling attacks. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-63718)\n\nHyojae Lee discovered that Apache HTTP Server did not properly validate\nDigest authentication requests. A machine-in-the-middle attacker could\npossibly use this issue to bypass authentication. (CVE-2026-73636)\n\nZhen Kong and Darren Carreras discovered that Apache HTTP Server did not\nproperly manage authentication requests. A remote attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-73637)\n\nVlatko Kosturjak discovered that Apache HTTP Server did not properly\nenforce access restrictions for user directories. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-79768)\n\nZhen Kong discovered that Apache HTTP Server did not properly handle\ncertain WebDAV requests. An authenticated user could possibly use this\nissue to cause a denial of service or corrupt WebDAV property data.\n(CVE-2026-93546)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"bionic":[{"name":"apache2","version":"2.4.29-1ubuntu4.27+esm13","description":"Apache HTTP server","is_source":true},{"name":"apache2","version":"2.4.29-1ubuntu4.27+esm13","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/apache2","version_link":null,"pocket":"esm-infra"},{"name":"apache2-bin","version":"2.4.29-1ubuntu4.27+esm13","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launc